title: 7. Why a part is done only with its evidence
pid: 313a26c2-aa2c-4348-96b2-b575e6a0c623
body: |2-
  Top reads the builder's report and the plan's state, not the code.
  First use: every builder gave its commands and their output, and
  building changed the wire form in four ways, each amended where the
  decision stood.
  Rests on: read (Anthropic's long-running harnesses: agents declare
  victory early, so a part is marked passing only after testing it as
  a user would, and builders do not edit the list of parts; Claude
  Code's best practices: ask for evidence).
